Page Name: Forum Journey
Slug: forum-journey

What it is: The pre-event page a registered Forum participant lands on between
registering and Day One. It counts down to the event, tells them the three
things they need to do this week (add to calendar, run a tech check, complete
their Information Form), walks them through the weekend's shape, and answers the
questions people ask before they arrive.

Who it is visible to: Registered Forum participants. The page is personalised
per registration -- the URL carries a unique id (/journey-XXXXXXX), and Ontraport
merges that registration's data into the page. No login is required: the URL
itself is the key, which is why no real journey URL is written down in this
public repo. Anyone holding one can read that participant's name, email and
phone straight off the page.

Where it lives: Ontraport Dynamic Page, template "Forum Journey" (page_122 on
the Registrations object, 10001). A registration's own URL is in its
"Forum Journey URL" field.

Live example: pull a current URL from the "Forum Journey URL" field on any
registration record in Ontraport. Do not paste one back into this repo.

Related pages: the same three "things to do" cards appear on the Member Portal
home page. That build renders the completed state slightly differently -- see
structure-map, "Known issues".
